# Web dashboard configuration.
#
# Every variable here is NEXT_PUBLIC_*, which means it is compiled into the
# browser bundle and visible to anyone who opens the page. That is the complete
# list of what this client is allowed to know.
#
# NEVER add to this file, or to any .env under apps/web:
#
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY  - bypasses row-level security. In a browser
#                                bundle it is a full database handover.
#   DATABASE_URL               - the web app has no driver and no business
#                                reading the database directly.
#   any courier API key        - those live encrypted in the backend vault and
#                                are never returned by any endpoint.
#
# The anon key below is safe by design: it is a public identifier that grants
# nothing on its own, and every business call goes to FastAPI carrying the
# signed-in session's JWT, which the API verifies.

# Supabase, used for authentication only. No table in this project is ever
# queried from the browser.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# The FastAPI the mobile app already uses. Include the version prefix.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com/v1
